  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">While there has been a decline in violent conflict and related humanitarian needs since the signing of the UN-facilitated Ceasefire Agreement in October 2020, political uncertainty, instability, criminality, weak governance structures, lack of social cohesion, limited economic opportunities and localized conflicts have continued to challenge sustained peace in southern Libya. Nationwide youth-led protests in July 2022 against the political and socio-economic situation in the country was a stark</narrative>
  </description>
